  "meta": {
    "probe": "rave-flyer-b",
    "target": "same target as rave-flyer, opposite economics: a one-colour handbill photocopied onto coloured stock, rather than a saturated colour printed on black",
    "method": "one ink on tinted ground, so the only decisions available are size, mass and where the black stops. The disc is clip-wrapped so it tessellates at 64 segments rather than 25, and the radial ticks are a ring layout, which is the only placement the substrate has that is not a grid or a line",
    "notDone": "the headline still cannot be condensed or stretched -- `transform.scale` is uniform and there is no skew -- so the display type is set at the proportions the face happens to have, which is the one thing no real flyer of this kind would accept"
  },
